cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "When does Claude tell you to go to sleep? A small study prompted by Fortune's story (fortune-asks-why-is-claude-telling-users-to-go-to-sleep-anthropic-ai-sentient)"
abstract: >-
  Long synthetic working sessions were given to Claude Opus 4.6 with its published claude.ai system prompt, and
  to seven other model setups, to measure when a model suggests rest, whether a stated reason is needed, and whether
  the suggestion returns after the person says no. Code, sessions, every reply, blind scores from two model families,
  and the cost ledger are included.
